# Shell scripts and the Dockerfile must keep LF endings.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows, where git checks files out with CRLF. A
# shell script whose shebang ends in \r fails inside a Linux container with the
# useless error "no such file or directory" — pointing at the interpreter, not
# the line ending. Forcing LF here means the Render build works regardless of
# who checked the file out.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
docker/* text eol=lf
